From: Pehacorp Kernel Optimization <kernel@pehacorp.local>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 07:33:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7921: optimize MT7922 throughput, ASPM, RX ring size and TX power headroom

Disable ASPM by default for MT7922 PCI wireless controllers to avoid PCIe L1/L1ss
latency spikes, and report the regulatory-limited max txpower of the active
channel in mt76_get_txpower instead of only the raw hardware calibration value.

NOTE: the RX_RING_SIZE bump to 4096 was reverted (2026-07-24) - it reliably
caused 4-way handshake timeouts (reason 15) on every association attempt,
while the same kernel without it held a wifi connection for 27+ minutes.
Keep at the stock 1536 until the ring-size regression is root-caused upstream.

Signed-off-by: Pehacorp Kernel Optimization <kernel@pehacorp.local>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/pci.c
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 	{ },
 };

-static bool mt7921_disable_aspm;
+static bool mt7921_disable_aspm = true;
 module_param_named(disable_aspm, mt7921_disable_aspm, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(disable_aspm, "disable PCI ASPM support");

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mac80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mac80211.c
@@ -1794,6 +1794,11 @@
 	if (!phy)
 		return -EINVAL;

+	if (phy->main_chandef.chan && phy->main_chandef.chan->max_power > 0) {
+		*dbm = phy->main_chandef.chan->max_power;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	n_chains = hweight16(phy->chainmask);
 	delta = mt76_tx_power_path_delta(n_chains);
 	*dbm = DIV_ROUND_UP(phy->txpower_cur + delta, 2);
